{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/124464-minor-endowment-question","id":124464,"title":"Minor Endowment Question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-03T06:56:22-07:00","id":124464,"title":"Minor Endowment Question","content":"The question's pretty simple: if we have a Malleus Maleficarum member use the Wrathful Sword of St. Michael Archangel and score, let's say, two successes, then deal three damage when she swings the blessed weapon at a supernatural creature, does the attack deal two Aggravated levels of damage and one Lethal (or Bashing, if the hunter is attacking a vampire) level, or just two Aggravated before it falls to pieces?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T10:18:36-07:00","id":128348,"title":"","content":"No answer, then? I'm leaning towards the former option by myself, so I guess that's what I'll do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T04:22:41-07:00","id":128867,"title":"","content":"I lean toward the second interpretation myself, but the ruling isn't really clear. I like the idea of the weapon disintegrating in mid strike, instead of afterwards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T07:56:06-07:00","id":128952,"title":"","content":"I suppose it comes down to whether you feel like a merciful Storyteller, in which case you'll go with Option #1, or not so merciful, which brings us to Option #2. Reverse that if the hunter in question is an antagonist, which is potentially the case for my chronicle. Without one of the writers making a statement, we probably won't get anything much more decisive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}